Add missing FIEMAP_EXTENT_* constants for loongarch64

linux-raw-sys generates loongarch64 ioctl bindings from a static snapshot
(gen/ioctl/loongarch-ioctls.txt) instead of the bindgen pipeline, and that
snapshot predates the FIEMAP constants. Only FS_IOC_FIEMAP is present, so
uv-fs fails with E0432 unresolved imports for the FIEMAP_EXTENT_* flags.

These are plain u32 bit flags from include/uapi/linux/fiemap.h and are
identical on every architecture; values match src/x86_64/ioctl.rs.
FIEMAP_MAX_OFFSET and FIEMAP_FLAG_* are deliberately omitted — uv does not
use them and FIEMAP_MAX_OFFSET's generated type varies.

Applied to the vendored linux-raw-sys crate, not to $builddir, hence the
.patchsrc extension (default_prepare only auto-applies *.patch).

Patch-Source: https://github.com/sunfishcode/linux-raw-sys/pull/195
Patch-Source: https://github.com/sunfishcode/linux-raw-sys/issues/192
--- a/src/loongarch64/ioctl.rs
+++ b/src/loongarch64/ioctl.rs
@@ -237,6 +237,17 @@
 pub const FS_IOC_GETVERSION: u32 = 2148038145;
 pub const FS_IOC_SETVERSION: u32 = 1074296322;
 pub const FS_IOC_FIEMAP: u32 = 3223348747;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_LAST: u32 = 1;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_UNKNOWN: u32 = 2;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_DELALLOC: u32 = 4;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_ENCODED: u32 = 8;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_DATA_ENCRYPTED: u32 = 128;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_NOT_ALIGNED: u32 = 256;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_DATA_INLINE: u32 = 512;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_DATA_TAIL: u32 = 1024;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_UNWRITTEN: u32 = 2048;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_MERGED: u32 = 4096;
+pub const FIEMAP_EXTENT_SHARED: u32 = 8192;
 pub const FS_IOC32_GETFLAGS: u32 = 2147771905;
 pub const FS_IOC32_SETFLAGS: u32 = 1074030082;
 pub const FS_IOC32_GETVERSION: u32 = 2147776001;
